    "updated_at": "2026-06-02T16:01:43Z",
    "body": "I propose doing the following.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIn 4.4.16 The div element;\r\n```\r\nCategories:\r\n    Flow content.\r\n    Palpable content.\r\nContexts in which this element can be used:\r\n    Where flow content is expected.\r\n    As a child of a dl element.\r\n    As a child of a select element.\r\n    As a child of a optgroup element.\r\n    As a child of a option element.\r\nContent model:\r\n    If the element is a child of a dl element: One or more dt elements followed by one or more dd elements, optionally intermixed with script-supporting elements.\r\n    Otherwise, if the element is a descendant of an option element: transparent.\r\n    Otherwise, if the element is a descendant of an optgroup element: transparent.\r\n    Otherwise, if the element is a descendant of a select element: transparent.\r\n    Otherwise: flow content.\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nWe remove the category of \"select element inner content elements\", \"optgroup element inner content elements\" & \"option element inner content elements\".\r\n\r\n\r\nIn 4.10.7 The select element;\r\n```\r\nContent model:\r\n    Zero or one button elements if the select is a drop-down box, followed by zero or more option, optgroup, hr, script-supporting elements, noscript or div.\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nIn 4.10.9 The optgroup element;\r\n```\r\nCategories:\r\n    None.\r\nContexts in which this element can be used:\r\n    As a child of a select element.\r\nContent model:\r\n    Zero or one legend element followed by option, script-supporting elements, noscript or div.\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nIn 4.10.10 The option element;\r\n```\r\nCategories:\r\n    None.\r\nContexts in which this element can be used:\r\n    As a child of a select element.\r\n    As a child of a datalist element.\r\n    As a child of an optgroup element.\r\nContent model:\r\n    If the element has a label attribute and a value attribute: Nothing.\r\n    If the element has a label attribute but no value attribute: Text.\r\n    If the element has no label attribute and is not a descendant of a datalist element: Zero or more div or phrasing content, but there must be no interactive content descendant, datalist element descendant, object element descendant, or descendant with the tabindex attribute specified\r\n    If the element has no label attribute and is a descendant of a datalist element: Text.\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nIn 4.4.2 The hr element;\r\n```\r\nCategories:\r\n    Flow content.\r\nContexts in which this element can be used:\r\n    Where flow content is expected.\r\n    As a child of a select element.\r\n```\r\n",
